@startuml comp-02-zero-trust-layers
title Phase 2 — Zero-Trust Security Layers

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageBorderColor #888888

package "Layer A — Platform RBAC (DONE ✅)" #E8F5E9 {
  [Keycloak OIDC\nJWT issuer\nComposite RBAC] as KC
  [Gateway SecurityConfig\nJWT validation\nPERM_* RBAC\nRoute-level authz] as GWSec
  [AuditGatewayFilter\nEvery write captured\nfire-and-forget] as AGF
  [Audit Service :9009\nImmutable trail\nNo seed / real data] as AuditSvc
  [Rate Limiting :9004\nRedis token bucket\nFail-open design] as RL
  [Anomaly Detection :9003\nRule-based + z-score\nATK-01 flood\nATK-02 IMSI enum] as AD
}

package "Layer B — 5G SBI Zero Trust (PLANNED 🔲)" #FFF9C4 {
  [free5GC NRF\nNF registry\nOAuth2 AS\nScoped SBI tokens\n(TS 33.501 §13)] as NRF
  [SBI TLS\nHTTPS on all NF\nSBI interfaces\nCert per NF] as SBI_TLS
  [mTLS Mesh\n(Istio/Linkerd/Cilium)\nPeer cert per container\nAMF↛UPF denied] as MTLS
  [PKI\nCFSSL or cert-manager\nSelf-signed CA\nLeaf certs per NF] as PKI
  [Grafana D5\nHandshake failures\nToken scope rejects\nCert expiry alert] as D5
}

KC --> GWSec : JWK set\n(RS256 validation)
GWSec --> AGF : SecurityContext\n(reactor)
AGF --> AuditSvc : write actions
GWSec --> RL : advisory check
AD --> RL : anomaly signals

NRF --> SBI_TLS : OAuth2 token\n+ TLS client cert
PKI --> SBI_TLS : issue leaf certs
PKI --> MTLS : issue workload certs
SBI_TLS --> MTLS : mTLS on top of TLS
MTLS --> D5 : metric: handshake failures
NRF --> D5 : metric: token scope rejects

note bottom of "Layer B — 5G SBI Zero Trust (PLANNED 🔲)" : Requires Linux host (Ubuntu 22.04 VM or WSL2)\nwith gtp5g kernel module for free5GC UPF.\nControl-plane NFs work on Windows (no UPF).

@enduml
